From: Local patch <local@local>
Date: Wed, 18 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: ucsi: make GET_CABLE_PROPERTY failure non-fatal

Some firmware implementations (e.g. AMD Phoenix / Framework 13 AMD)
return "unrecognized command" (error 0 or 256) for GET_CABLE_PROPERTY,
even though the UCSI_CAP_CABLE_DETAILS feature bit is set. This causes
ucsi_register_cable() to abort, which prevents the UCSI connection
sequence from completing and the USB data path from being enabled on the
port, leaving USB devices plugged directly into USB-C invisible to xHCI.

Rather than propagating the error, fall back to registering a generic
passive USB-C cable so the connection sequence can complete normally.

Signed-off-by: Local patch <local@local>
---
 drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c b/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c
@@ -937,8 +937,9 @@
 	command = UCSI_GET_CABLE_PROPERTY | UCSI_CONNECTOR_NUMBER(con->num);
 	ret = ucsi_send_command(con->ucsi, command, &cable_prop, sizeof(cable_prop));
 	if (ret < 0) {
-		dev_err(con->ucsi->dev, "GET_CABLE_PROPERTY failed (%d)\n", ret);
-		return ret;
+		dev_warn(con->ucsi->dev, "GET_CABLE_PROPERTY failed (%d), assuming passive USB-C cable\n", ret);
+		desc.type = USB_PLUG_TYPE_C;
+		goto register_cable;
 	}

 	switch (UCSI_CABLE_PROP_FLAG_PLUG_TYPE(cable_prop.flags)) {
@@ -963,6 +964,7 @@
 	if (con->ucsi->version >= UCSI_VERSION_2_1)
 		desc.pd_revision = UCSI_CABLE_PROP_FLAG_PD_MAJOR_REV_AS_BCD(cable_prop.flags);

+register_cable:
 	cable = typec_register_cable(con->port, &desc);
 	if (IS_ERR(cable)) {
 		dev_err(con->ucsi->dev,
